  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nZonal to northwest flow will set up in the upper levels over the \nweekend with a couple of shortwave troughs coming through Saturday \nevening and again Wednesday. Low moisture content will mean these \nfrontal passages will be dry with an increase in upper level clouds \nand a northerly shift in the winds being the main impacts. \nOtherwise, skies will be mostly clear and winds should remain light \nwith high pressure setting in for the week. Temperatures will be \nseasonable with highs in the 60s to 70s and lows in the 40s to 50s \nthrough Tuesday. The shortwave features on Wednesday will bring some \nwarm air advection from the Desert SW which will increase temps a \nbit through the later half of the week, with highs in the mid 70s \nand lows in the mid 50s.",
